What will you do if there is a production issue but you are unable to reproduce it in lower environments

If I am unable to reproduce the issue in a lower environment, I would first focus on collecting as much information 
as possible from production.

I would start by checking application logs, API logs, error messages, user details, request payloads, and any monitoring tools 
available.

Next, I would compare the production environment with lower environments to identify differences in configuration, data, 
user roles, permissions, feature flags, or third-party integrations.

Since many production issues are data-specific, I would try to identify whether the issue is affecting only certain users, 
roles, or specific business scenarios



If needed, I would work with the support team or affected users to gather exact steps, screenshots, and request details.

Based on the findings, I would create a similar test scenario in a lower environment or use production-like test data to reproduce the issue.

If the issue is critical and the root cause is still unclear, I would collaborate with backend, DevOps, and other teams to 
analyze logs and narrow down the problem while keeping stakeholders informed about progress.

My goal would be to minimize user impact while systematically identifying the root cause.

