One challenging technical issue I faced was after a production deployment when some users were unable to log in to our application.

Since our project was supporting US users, deployments usually happened during their nighttime. 
We needed to resolve the issue before users started accessing the application the next morning.

First, I joined the incident bridge call with the team to understand the impact and identify which users were affected. 
I checked the application logs, API responses, and recent deployment changes.

During the investigation, we identified an issue related to role-based authorization. 
The backend was returning user role and access information that did not match the frontend's authorization validation, 
which prevented certain users from logging in successfully.

I coordinated with the backend team to identify the root cause and reproduced the issue using different user roles 
in a lower environment. After identifying the required changes, we tested the fix and validated the login flow for different roles.

Once the fix was verified, we deployed the hotfix and monitored the application to ensure users could log in successfully.

We resolved the issue before the next business day. Afterward, we added additional test cases for different user roles 
and improved validation to prevent similar issues in future deployments.

This experience taught me the importance of systematic debugging, cross-team collaboration, and having proper regression 
testing for critical functionality such as authentication.


